      "file": "WT004_reinitialisation/registry.rs",
      "id": "410ab9cbe9e9fbf2",
      "item_path": "CreateProfile.profile",
      "line": 37,
      "message": "`CreateProfile.profile` uses `init_if_needed` on program state, and no handler checks whether the account already holds data. A caller can pass an existing account and have the handler overwrite state that belongs to someone else.",
      "references": [
        "https://solana.com/developers/courses/program-security/reinitialization-attacks",
        "https://www.anchor-lang.com/docs/account-constraints"
      ],
      "remediation": "Ask whether the account is already initialised before writing the fields that establish ownership — compare the stored authority against `Pubkey::default()`, or require it to match the caller. Where creation and update are genuinely different operations, give them separate instructions and use plain `init`.",
      "rule": "WT004",
      "severity": "high",
      "snippet": "    pub profile: Account<'info, Profile>,"
    },
    {
      "column": 9,
      "confidence": "medium",
      "file": "WT005_missing_has_one/treasury.rs",
      "id": "0dc13ff4575e2169",
      "item_path": "Withdraw.treasury",
      "line": 33,
      "message": "`Treasury` stores `authority: Pubkey`, and `Withdraw` takes both `treasury` and `authority`, but never checks that they match. The stored key records a relationship the instruction does not enforce, so any `treasury` can be used with any `authority`.",
      "references": [
        "https://solana.com/developers/courses/program-security/account-data-matching",
        "https://www.anchor-lang.com/docs/account-constraints"
      ],
      "remediation": "Add `has_one = <field>` to the account that stores the key, or assert it explicitly with `constraint = account.field == other.key()`. Deriving the account's address from the key with `seeds` enforces the same relationship and is stronger still.",
      "rule": "WT005",
      "severity": "high",
      "snippet": "    pub treasury: Account<'info, Treasury>,"
    },
    {
      "column": 9,
      "confidence": "high",
      "file": "WT006_non_canonical_bump/market.rs",
      "id": "f8c3eb4d2afe9cab",
      "item_path": "OpenMarket.market",
      "line": 38,
      "message": "`OpenMarket.market` derives its address with `bump = market_bump`, which comes from the instruction argument `market_bump`. The caller chooses the bump, so they can derive several valid addresses for the same seeds. Use a bare `bump` and let Anchor supply the canonical one.",
      "references": [
        "https://solana.com/developers/courses/program-security/bump-seed-canonicalization",
        "https://www.anchor-lang.com/docs/pdas"
      ],
      "remediation": "Write `bump` on its own and let Anchor derive the canonical bump, storing `ctx.bumps.<account>` if later instructions need it. Where a bump is re-derived, read it from the account (`bump = account.bump`) rather than from the caller.",
      "rule": "WT006",
      "severity": "high",
      "snippet": "        bump = market_bump,"
    },
