      "id": "54d2cd9bdf500a57",
      "item_path": "Claim.clock",
      "line": 43,
      "message": "`Claim.clock` is named for a sysvar but is an unchecked account with no address constraint. Sysvars live at fixed addresses and are otherwise ordinary accounts, so a caller can substitute one with contents of their choosing.",
      "references": [
        "https://solana.com/developers/courses/program-security/sysvar-spoofing",
        "https://docs.rs/anchor-lang/latest/anchor_lang/accounts/sysvar/struct.Sysvar.html"
      ],
      "remediation": "Use `Sysvar<'info, Clock>` and its siblings, which assert the address. For sysvars Anchor has no type for, pin it with `#[account(address = sysvar::instructions::ID)]`.",
      "rule": "WT009",
      "severity": "high",
      "snippet": "    pub clock: AccountInfo<'info>,"
    },
